WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:01.701
-We do not always

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:03.033
have enough time to cover all

00:00:03.033 --> 00:00:04.033
of the recent news,

00:00:04.033 --> 00:00:05.534
so here with a recap is one

00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:07.100
of our writers, Amber Ruffin,

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:09.567
in a segment we call
"Amber Says What."

00:00:09.567 --> 00:00:11.667
♪♪

00:00:11.667 --> 00:00:13.167
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Yay! You guys,

00:00:13.167 --> 00:00:15.434
things. have. been. crazy.

00:00:15.434 --> 00:00:18.334
Okay, so everyone was like,
"COVID is slowing down.

00:00:18.334 --> 00:00:19.767
You can hang out
with your friends."

00:00:19.767 --> 00:00:21.033
And I was like, "What?!"

00:00:21.033 --> 00:00:22.868
Then, Omicron hit
and they were like,

00:00:22.868 --> 00:00:24.133
"Stop hanging out
with your friends!"

00:00:24.133 --> 00:00:25.367
And I was like, "What?!"

00:00:25.367 --> 00:00:27.801
[ Laughter ]
Omicron got everybody,

00:00:27.801 --> 00:00:29.167
especially at late night.

00:00:29.167 --> 00:00:31.501
James Corden got it,
and I was like, "What?!"

00:00:31.567 --> 00:00:34.133
[ Laughter ]
Jimmy Fallon got it
and I was like, "What?!"

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:36.234
Then, Seth Meyers got it

00:00:36.234 --> 00:00:38.434
and I was like, "Wha-a-a-t?!"

00:00:38.434 --> 00:00:39.234
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:39.234 --> 00:00:40.067
Seth!

00:00:40.067 --> 00:00:41.868
Were you kissing Jimmy Fallon?

00:00:41.868 --> 00:00:44.534
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.534 --> 00:00:46.868
[ Fresh laughter, applause ]

00:00:46.868 --> 00:00:47.968
-[ Changes accent ]
Mind your business.

00:00:47.968 --> 00:00:49.601
[ Laughter ]
-I knew it!

00:00:49.601 --> 00:00:52.400
Then, while we were all working
from home,

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:54.267
everyone we love died,

00:00:54.267 --> 00:00:56.367
and I'm barely exaggerating.

00:00:56.367 --> 00:00:58.667
Betty White died
and I was like, "What?!"

00:00:58.667 --> 00:01:01.033
Sidney Poitier died and I was
like, "What?!"

00:01:01.033 --> 00:01:03.200
Then, Bob Saget died
and I was like,

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:04.801
"What?!
Oh, my gosh!

00:01:04.801 --> 00:01:06.801
[ Striking palm ]
All of our favorites are dying!"

00:01:06.801 --> 00:01:09.167
Then, Robert Durst was like,
"I died, too,"

00:01:09.167 --> 00:01:10.567
and I was like, "No!

00:01:10.567 --> 00:01:11.534
[ Laughter ]
Robert Durst,

00:01:11.534 --> 00:01:13.300
this is not about you!

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:14.667
Do not try to sneak in there

00:01:14.667 --> 00:01:16.234
while we're mourning
beloved Americans.

00:01:16.234 --> 00:01:17.968
Shame on you!"
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.968 --> 00:01:20.901
Then, Machine Gun Kelly
and Megan Fox got engaged

00:01:20.901 --> 00:01:21.901
[ Cheering ]
and I was like, "What?!

00:01:21.901 --> 00:01:23.334
That's fantastic!

00:01:23.334 --> 00:01:25.367
I, for one,
cannot wait to see pictures

00:01:25.367 --> 00:01:27.934
of their smooth,
angular children.

00:01:27.934 --> 00:01:29.501
[ Laughter ]
Then I read about it

00:01:29.501 --> 00:01:30.868
and they were like,
"We got engaged

00:01:30.868 --> 00:01:32.667
and then we drank
each other's blood,"

00:01:32.667 --> 00:01:35.467
and I was like, "What?!
[ Laughter ]

00:01:35.467 --> 00:01:38.167
Why do you have
to ruin everything?

00:01:38.167 --> 00:01:40.067
You don't need
each other's blood.

00:01:40.067 --> 00:01:41.667
What is wrong with you?!

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:44.334
You might [bleep] around
and get a taste for human blood.

00:01:44.334 --> 00:01:45.334
Is that what you want?"

00:01:45.334 --> 00:01:46.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:47.501
Just reckless!

00:01:47.501 --> 00:01:49.734
I wouldn't let someone drink
some of my margarita,

00:01:49.734 --> 00:01:51.534
let alone some of my blood,

00:01:51.534 --> 00:01:54.234
which, by the way,
is mostly margarita.

00:01:54.234 --> 00:01:57.801
[ Laughter ]
Then, something
horrible happened.

00:01:57.801 --> 00:02:00.167
Jason Momoa and Lisa Monet split

00:02:00.167 --> 00:02:02.467
after being together
for 16 years

00:02:02.467 --> 00:02:03.767
and I was like, "What?!

00:02:03.767 --> 00:02:05.200
I'm devastated!"

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:07.300
But not for them, for me.

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:09.200
[ Laughter ]
Like all Americans,

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:11.534
I desperately wanted them
to make me the third

00:02:11.534 --> 00:02:13.501
in their open marriage
[ Laughter ]

00:02:13.501 --> 00:02:15.868
and now I am in mourning.

00:02:15.868 --> 00:02:17.300
"Did somebody say mourning?"

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:19.801
Not now, Robert Durst!
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:19.801 --> 00:02:21.667
Also, let's talk
about Lisa Bonet's

00:02:21.667 --> 00:02:23.267
extremely high standards.

00:02:23.267 --> 00:02:25.100
She married Lenny Kravitz

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:26.968
and then Jason Momoa.

00:02:26.968 --> 00:02:28.400
Who is she going to marry next,

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:29.801
a beam of light?

00:02:29.801 --> 00:02:31.767
[ Laughter ]
Lucky beam of light.

00:02:31.767 --> 00:02:34.901
Then, New York Mayor Eric Adams
hired his brother

00:02:34.901 --> 00:02:36.234
to be in charge of security.

00:02:36.234 --> 00:02:38.200
and everyone was like,
"Wha-a-a-t?!"

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:39.501
But I was like, "What?"

00:02:39.501 --> 00:02:42.501
My sister Lacey is the head
of my security detail.

00:02:42.501 --> 00:02:44.767
She's keeping me secure
right now.

00:02:44.767 --> 00:02:47.234
-Hey! You want me
to throw this guy out of here?

00:02:47.234 --> 00:02:48.601
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:49.734
-It's my show!

00:02:49.734 --> 00:02:52.000
-No, Lacey,
he's my little friend.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:52.734
-Oh, yay!
[ Claps ]

00:02:52.734 --> 00:02:54.667
-[Both, clapping] Yay!

00:02:54.667 --> 00:02:55.934
[ Laughter and applause ]
-Then,

00:02:55.934 --> 00:02:57.400
the Golden Globes happened

00:02:57.400 --> 00:02:59.501
and that was like,
"What, where, when,

00:02:59.501 --> 00:03:01.634
and, most importantly, what?!"

00:03:01.634 --> 00:03:04.434
Why was it a secret and who won?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.434 --> 00:03:06.601
I looked it up and you're
never going to believe it.

00:03:06.601 --> 00:03:08.801
Best Actress?
Amber Mildred Ruffin.

00:03:08.801 --> 00:03:11.133
[ Laughter ]
And then Best Supporting Actress
went to

00:03:11.133 --> 00:03:12.501
Amber Mildred Ruffin.

00:03:12.501 --> 00:03:14.467
Best Late Night segment went to

00:03:14.467 --> 00:03:16.767
"Amber Says What,"
which beat "A Closer Look"

00:03:16.767 --> 00:03:19.167
by 6,547 votes.

00:03:19.167 --> 00:03:20.434
-Hey!

00:03:20.434 --> 00:03:21.801
-Don't make me throw you
out of here.

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:23.200
-Alright, okay.

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:25.100
Okay, Lacey.

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:27.300
[ Laughter ]
-Then, speaking of award shows,

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:30.167
okay, so, after three years
of going without a host,

00:03:30.167 --> 00:03:32.901
the Oscars are finally going
to get one!

00:03:32.901 --> 00:03:34.501
[ Cheering and applause ]
Yay!

00:03:34.501 --> 00:03:36.601
And, as the winner
of the Golden Globe

00:03:36.601 --> 00:03:37.801
for Hostiest Host,

00:03:37.801 --> 00:03:39.567
I think I should be
the one to do it.

00:03:39.567 --> 00:03:42.100
Shoot, if Christian Siriano
makes me a dress,

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:44.267
I'll do that [bleep] for free!

00:03:44.267 --> 00:03:46.133
[ Laughter ]
Hear me, Christian? Call me!

00:03:46.133 --> 00:03:48.667
Then, you will never guess
what happened.

00:03:48.667 --> 00:03:51.701
They put Maya Angelou
on the quarter!

00:03:51.701 --> 00:03:52.801
[ Cheering ]
I saw that and was like,

00:03:52.801 --> 00:03:54.200
"What-what?! Yes!"

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:55.834
They put a woman on the quarter.

00:03:55.834 --> 00:03:58.033
It better not be worth 20 cents.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:58.033 --> 00:04:01.467
Now, I cannot wait to get
my Maya Angelou quarter.

00:04:01.467 --> 00:04:03.734
It really is like she
always said --

00:04:03.734 --> 00:04:06.334
[ As Angelou ]
People will forget
what you said.

00:04:06.334 --> 00:04:09.234
People will forget what you did.

00:04:09.234 --> 00:04:11.367
But people will never forget

00:04:11.367 --> 00:04:14.968
you're on a shiny coin
in their pocket.

00:04:14.968 --> 00:04:19.000
[ Laughter ]
Then, the FDA deregulated

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:22.167
French dressing
and I was like, "What?

00:04:22.167 --> 00:04:22.968
[ Laughter ]

00:04:22.968 --> 00:04:24.234
Why were they regulating

00:04:24.234 --> 00:04:25.934
French dressing,
in the first place?"

00:04:25.934 --> 00:04:27.934
So, it turns out there were
certain ingredients

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:29.801
you had to have to qualify
as French dressing,

00:04:29.801 --> 00:04:31.934
but now, anything goes!

00:04:31.934 --> 00:04:33.767
[ Laughter ]
And I'm like, "Whoo! What?!

00:04:33.767 --> 00:04:35.934
What are they going to put
in it, something illegal?"

00:04:35.934 --> 00:04:38.467
So, if that's true, I demand

00:04:38.467 --> 00:04:39.834
[ Striking palm ]
the illegal version.

00:04:39.834 --> 00:04:43.667
It is my right to have pure,
uncut French dressing,

00:04:43.667 --> 00:04:45.234
and I'll settle
for nothing less!

00:04:45.234 --> 00:04:47.200
[ Laughter and applause ]
Then, I found out

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:49.367
that a huge asteroid
is going to pass

00:04:49.367 --> 00:04:51.701
extremely close to Earth today

00:04:51.701 --> 00:04:53.033
and I was like, "What?!"

00:04:53.033 --> 00:04:54.734
And I just want to say that,

00:04:54.734 --> 00:04:56.734
if this is our last day
of existence,

00:04:56.734 --> 00:04:59.167
I'mma be so sad
because I don't want to die

00:04:59.167 --> 00:05:00.133
[ Slapping thighs ]
without trying that

00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:02.000
uncut French dressing!

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:03.534
[ Laughter ]
I want it!

00:05:03.534 --> 00:05:06.734
Then, I watched the new season
of "Euphoria"

00:05:06.734 --> 00:05:08.033
[ Cheering and applause ]
and I was like,

00:05:08.033 --> 00:05:09.667
"Wha-wha-now!"

00:05:09.667 --> 00:05:12.100
I was like,
"What a smart decision I made

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:13.634
to not have children."

00:05:13.634 --> 00:05:16.300
[ Laughter ]
Those gross little children.

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:18.767
The only thing those babies
should be putting up their noses

00:05:18.767 --> 00:05:20.234
is a COVID test.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.234 --> 00:05:22.501
Then, everyone has been
doing bits about "Euphoria"

00:05:22.501 --> 00:05:24.634
on Twitter, talking about how
those kids dress, like,

00:05:24.634 --> 00:05:26.267
"This is how I dress for school"

00:05:26.267 --> 00:05:27.634
and then it's them
in normal clothes.

00:05:27.634 --> 00:05:29.067
And then they're like,
"This is how I dress

00:05:29.067 --> 00:05:30.701
for school at Euphoria High,"

00:05:30.701 --> 00:05:32.200
[ Laughter ]
and it's them dressed
to go to the club.

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:34.067
And all those were so funny

00:05:34.067 --> 00:05:35.434
that we were going to do
a bit about it,

00:05:35.434 --> 00:05:38.000
but then I decided, we're not.

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:39.067
-We're not?

00:05:39.067 --> 00:05:40.601
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:40.601 --> 00:05:42.167
-No.

00:05:42.167 --> 00:05:43.767
-Well, why didn't you tell me?

00:05:43.767 --> 00:05:45.501
-That's it, you're outta here.
-Alright.

00:05:45.501 --> 00:05:47.334
[ Laughter ]
-This has been...

00:05:47.334 --> 00:05:50.734
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:05:50.734 --> 00:05:52.100
-Amber Ruffin, everyone!

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:54.701
Check out "The Amber Ruffin
Show" on Peacock.

00:05:54.701 --> 00:05:57.067
New episodes return
after the Olympics.

00:05:57.067 --> 00:05:58.968
We'll be --
I just have to do this part!

00:05:58.968 --> 00:06:00.634
We'll be right back
with Jeremy Irons.

00:06:00.634 --> 00:06:02.367
-I said, go!
-Alright, I'm going!

00:06:02.367 --> 00:06:04.634
♪♪

